+detector or background-physics correlation length. Likewise, the lower and upper
+values in Eq.~\eqref{eq:dataset-lengthscale-bounds} define the numerical optimizer
+domain. An optimum at $\ell_{\max}$ establishes that the constraint is active for
+that fit, not that the physical background correlation scale has been measured at
+the boundary. The implementation optimizes log-transformed kernel
+hyperparameters within these configured bounds \cite{ScikitLearnGPRDocs16}.
